  "handle": "Parsimony#05d5",
  "mechanism": "Acts as a Judge#f7d5 to evaluate Topology#2408 necessity (Occam's Razor). Classifies complexity into three qualitative states: (1) Bloated: Core concept collapses or remains identical without this component. (2) Under-specified: Plausible utility, but necessity is not strictly proven via ablation. (3) Minimal: Proven essential; removing any part destroys the function. Aims for high Compress#0967ion.",
  "invariants": [
    "Necessity: Every component must have a causal link to the outcome."
  ],
  "signature": [
    "Judge(Topology)"
